<title>USA: Allstar Inns Inc Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Allstar Inns Inc Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA BARBARA, Calif. 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>						  Quarter Ended March 31,</p>
<p>								1997     1996</p>
<p>Revenues:</p>
<p>   Rent income					 $  1,839$  8,604</p>
<p>   Interest income					  480     207</p>
<p>     Total revenues				     2,319   8,811</p>
<p>Expenses:</p>
<p>   Administrative and general			 4,119     285</p>
<p>Depreciation &amp; amortization and other expense</p>
<p>								1,207   2,229</p>
<p>   Gain from sale of assets		     (116,408)	--</p>
<p>     Total expenses				 (111,082)   2,514</p>
<p> Operating income				     113,401   6,297</p>
<p> Interest expense					 1,508   4,803</p>
<p>Net income before provision for income taxes</p>
<p>							    111,893   1,494</p>
<p> Provision (benefit) for income taxes	    45,094   (449)</p>
<p> Net income						66,799   1,943</p>
<p> Net income per common share			  63.77    1.97</p>
<p> Weighted average common shares outstanding     1,047     985</p>
<p>Pursuant to the Master Lease Agreement, as approved by the stockholders at the company's 1995 Annual Meeting, effective as of Jan. 30, 1997, all of the company's motels (71 motels with 7,606 rooms) were sold to Motel 6 Operating L.P. and its assignees.  As of April 29, 1997, the company now holds only two parcels of unimproved land which the company intends to sell for cash.  The company will be subject to substantial Federal and State taxes on the gain realized by the sale of the motel assets. On March 14, 1997, the board of directors adopted a Plan of Complete Liquidation and Dissolution of the company which will be presented to the company's stockholders for approval at the company's annual meeting to be held on May 8, 1997 in Montecito, Calif.</p>
